---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About | Nether"
  description="Meet HADES and learn what Nether covers: web development, AI tools, keyboards, mice, and IEMs."
>
  <main class="archive-page plain-page">
    <header class="archive-header">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p>
        I’m HADES, the writer and builder behind Nether. I made this site to
        explain the tools and trade-offs behind modern web work, and to make
        technical gear easier to compare without reducing it to a spec sheet.
      </p>
    </header>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>What I write about</h2>
      <p>
        My web development articles cover browser features, JavaScript, CSS,
        and practical decisions involved in building and maintaining a site. I
        also write about AI tools in development: where they help, how to check
        their output, and where careful human review still matters.
      </p>
      <p>
        The gear pages focus on keyboards, mice, and in-ear monitors (IEMs).
        I explain the terminology, strengths, and compromises that help readers
        compare products against their own preferences.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>How I cover gear</h2>
      <p>
        The gear data distinguishes hands-on ratings from scores based on
        specifications and reviewer consensus. I do not present a research
        score as personal testing. My category criteria, testing approach, and
        score meanings are explained in
        <a href="/gear/how-i-rate/">How I rate gear</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Across all topics, I aim to explain the question first, separate
        verifiable details from opinion, and make the relevant trade-offs
        understandable. A recommendation is context, not a claim that one
        choice is right for everyone.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Send feedback, corrections, or questions through the contact options
        shown on the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page. For information
        about store links and how gear ratings are made, see the
        <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure</a> and
        <a href="/gear/how-i-rate/">rating criteria</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
    <nav aria-label="More about this site" class="plain-page-links">
      <a href="/blog/">Web development and AI articles</a>
      <a href="/keyboards/">Keyboards</a>
      <a href="/mice/">Mice</a>
      <a href="/iems/">IEMs</a>
      <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
    </nav>
    <p class="legal-updated">
      Last updated <time datetime="2026-11-02">November 2, 2026</time>.
    </p>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
